From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:35:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: s2r: leave suspend-to-idle alone in
 ->begin()

platform_suspend_begin() calls suspend_ops->begin() for suspend-to-idle
too when no s2idle_ops are registered, and apple-s2r registers none. So
since apple-s2r offers suspend-to-RAM by default, every suspend-to-idle
also saved the AP pins and set pm_set_suspend_via_firmware(), telling
drivers the SoC would power down. The M4 GPU then refuses the sleep, and
a lid close on a J604 with a running desktop aborts instead of
suspending to idle.

Return early from ->begin() for anything but PM_SUSPEND_MEM.

Fixes: 64f6e57a6a37 ("soc: apple: s2r: offer suspend-to-RAM whenever the boot firmware opts in")
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c
index 3e7d0363fb..132a5b2923 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c
@@ -989,6 +989,12 @@ static void apple_s2r_wake(void)
  */
 static int apple_s2r_begin(suspend_state_t state)
 {
+	/*
+	 * With no s2idle_ops the PM core calls this for suspend-to-idle as
+	 * well: that one keeps the SoC powered, so leave it alone.
+	 */
+	if (state != PM_SUSPEND_MEM)
+		return 0;
 	if (apple_s2r)
 		apple_s2r_pins_save(apple_s2r);
 	pm_set_suspend_via_firmware();
